  "body": "Step E3 of #637: the app's stock holders carry stock through one engine-agnostic type, so a carried program can run on the field engine. The column engine stays the default, call for call - no shipped verdict, golden or stamp changes.\n\n## Design answers (full text in `docs/decisions/637-carried-stock-holders.md` and the [issue comment](https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/issues/637#issuecomment-6815368088))\n\n1. **Representation:** a transformed query frame, never a re-sample (the bake before a cut is a re-index on the origin-locked lattice). New here: the field arm builds its solid in the stock lattice's own frame (corner at the origin), so every verdict column is a field cell centre.\n2. **Floor:** the lower end of the column's one material interval (`column_span`). A column cut through used to read back as air (`-inf`), which a verdict reads as \"nothing to judge\". It now reads the stock's own extent (top at the stock's floor, floor at the stock's top, both finite), so the column stays empty and the verdict convicts it.\n3. **Clip:** the column law as a solid - the body minus the half-infinite prism above the entered stock's top over its footprint - not a plain intersection, which would delete material standing beside the new block (less material than the column engine reports).\n4. **Agreement lane:** sim pins in the quick lane, an app heavy lane over the three carried suites' fixtures, and a per-thread engine switch so one process reads both.\n\n## What changed\n\n- **camcraft-sim:** `CarriedStock` (`Column(Body)` | `Field(Box<FieldBody>)`) in `stock_sim/carried.rs`: `carry`, `simulate`, `clip_under`, `into_body`, `deviate`. `FieldBody::body` (`carried_read.rs`) reads the field back onto the column `Body`, so `deviate`, `display`, `volume` and `bounds` are the column carry's own code on both arms. `clip_columns_under` is the clip loop moved out of the app.\n- **camcraft-app:** `stock_sim_held.rs` holds `Held` (`Plain(Stock)` | `Carried(CarriedStock)`), `first_body` and the engine switch (`stock_sim::with_carry_engine`, `carry_engine`, env `CAMCRAFT_CARRY_ENGINE=field`). `stock_sim_carry::walk` / `judge` / `incoming_body`, `simulate_document`, `rest/across::sweep`, `rest::prior_state` and `rest::PriorPlan` go through it. The carried-body cache key takes the engine on the field arm only (the column key is unchanged).\n- A cylinder stock is refused by name on the field arm (`FIELD_CARRY_SHAPE_REFUSAL`): its mesh is an inscribed polygon and would hold less than the column engine's disc at the rim.\n- Old project files: nothing persisted changes.\n\n## Tests\n\n- `crates/sim/tests/carried_stock.rs` (6, quick lane): a block off the cell pitch on both arms - uncut, cut, carried through all 8 lattice turns and cut again, two carries with a cut between, the clip under a block and a round (then flipped and cut), a cut-through column convicted on both arms before and after a flip, degenerate field blocks refused.\n- `crates/app/tests/carried_engine_agreement.rs`: heavy lane `both_engines_read_every_carried_document_alike` (`#[ignore]`, release): 14 documents mirroring `setup_carry`, `rest_across_setups` and `carried_verify`; per document the program verdict, the incoming body, the rest grid, verify's prior, the entered body and verify's bounds are read on both engines. **0 findings, max |delta| 0 on every read, 54 s in release.** A mutation check (field tops raised 1e-3) made it fail on every document, so the lane is not vacuous. Plus `the_engine_switch_is_scoped_and_defaults_to_the_column_engine` in the default lane.\n- The carried suites run whole on the field arm (`CAMCRAFT_CARRY_ENGINE=field`): `setup_carry` 9/9, `rest_across_setups` 7/7, `carried_verify` 8/8, `carried_fixtures_cache` 6/6.\n- Gates on head 68d317b7 (Linux): `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main` green - sim suites 203 s, motion 11 s, every app suite 1009 s, 0 failed (it covers `setup_carry`, `rest_across_setups`, `carried_verify`, `carried_fixtures_cache`, `stock_sim_document`, `remachining`, `suppressed_rest`, `top_stock`, `setup_stock_source`, `stock_engine_agreement`). `cargo clippy -p camcraft-sim -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings` clean. Release heavy lanes: `carried_engine_agreement -- --ignored` 1/1 (54 s), `stock_engine_agreement -- --ignored` 3/3 (37 s).\n\n## Not exercised / known limits\n\n- Field arm only (not the shipped default): a cylinder stock is refused; a from-model stock is built (`FieldBody::mesh`) but no lane document uses one; ball, taper and bull-nose tools are not in the lane's documents (all flat end mills, which is why the deltas are exactly 0).\n- On a cut-through column the field arm reports the gouge depth to the stock's floor, not the tool's depth below it (the column engine's number). Same class, different magnitude; the sim pin states both. No lane document cuts through.\n- The field arm is slow in debug (the carried suites take 15-50 s each against under 1 s on the column arm); release is about 4 s per document.\n- The operation priors (`drill_prior`, `top_stock`, `carried_stock`) still receive the read-back tops as a `Dexel` through `Columns::of_grid`; removing `Dexel` from the app is #586's remaining work, and the default flip is #589.\n- No golden moved. No snapshot PNG touched. Windows and macOS not run.\n\nChangelog: none (refactor; the column engine remains the default and every shipped verdict is unchanged).\n\nEffort: max (not escalated). Fork synced at v0.18.0.\n\nRefs #637\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
